DroidVM kgsl fixes for the host driver.

gfxstream/venus (vk command proxy) executes the guest's Vulkan on this
turnip over kgsl on the host phone. Squash of Droid-VM/turnip gen8
486c9735e9d + b43c434e0f + bf2112ca28:

- kgsl: poll timestamps instead of blocking. A timeout of 0 means "wait
  indefinitely" to KGSL's WAITTIMESTAMP, so an already-expired deadline
  (every vk_sync_timeline GC poll) blocked up to a whole frame while
  holding the timeline mutex; 374 such calls were 556ms of a 588ms total
  under Minecraft. Read KGSL_TIMESTAMP_RETIRED instead (~12us).
- kgsl: track sparse VMAs in dump-bo list. kgsl_sparse_vma_init skipped
  tu_dump_bo_init, leaving dump_bo_list_idx 0 (not ~0); tu_dump_bo_del
  then dereferenced an empty dump_bo_list on free (crash on world-gen).
- kgsl: tolerate KHR_display instance extension. Clients like
  zink-on-weston-DRM enable it opportunistically yet drive scanout
  through GBM/dmabuf; rejecting instance creation broke that valid path.
  The physical-device display queries just report zero displays.

Context regenerated against mesa 7f196910eb35aca76cf58d0c572c72c099e971a2.

